module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.unread_member_defaults_to_a_legal_value_of_its_domain

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data unread_member_defaults_to_a_legal_value_of_its_domain: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "unread_member_defaults_to_a_legal_value_of_its_domain" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a decoder that cannot read a member substitutes a value the peer could legitimately have sent, so the gap becomes indistinguishable from data** (INVALID STATE: a decode arm for an absent, wrong-typed or unparseable member answers with an inhabitant of the member's own domain -- an empty object for arguments, an empty string for an identifier, zero for a count -- rather than with a refusal or a typed unavailability. HARM: every downstream consumer is reading a value that was never observed, and no consumer can tell, because the substituted value is exactly what a well-formed peer sends when it means that value. The wrongness is therefore SILENT in the DESIGN section 5 sense rather than merely lenient, and it is not caught by any amount of consumer-side care: there is nothing at the consumer to be careful about.)",

    "WHY IT IS ITS OWN CLASS AND NOT [[absorbing_fallback]]. The absorbing fallback widens -- it answers the SUPERSET, top-as-answer standing for top-as-ignorance -- and its cost is that it is denominated in the corpus rather than the change. This one NARROWS to a specific point of the domain, and its cost is that the point is indistinguishable from a measurement. The repairs are non-substitutable: an absorbing fallback is repaired by computing the precise set, and no precision repairs this one, because the deficit is that a value was invented at all. Nor is it [[refusal_reabsorbed_by_intermediate_default]], where a producer DID refuse correctly and a later frame swallowed it -- following the outcome through consumers is the guard there, and here there is no outcome to follow, because the producing site never made one.",

    "THE RECOGNITION RULE IS A QUESTION ABOUT THE DEFAULT'S MEMBERSHIP, NOT ABOUT ITS SIZE: ask whether a correct peer could send exactly this value meaning it. If it could, the default has no marker and the decode arm must refuse or return a typed unavailability instead. The empty collection, the empty string and zero are the three that pass review most easily, because each reads as neutral -- and neutrality is the property that makes them undetectable, not the property that makes them safe.",

    "THREE SPECIMENS IN ONE DECODER, FOUND BY OPERATOR-SUPPLIED SCOPE REVIEW AND CONFIRMED ON MAIN (2026-09-11, gunbc DSV41-3, `gunbc.harness.harness_wire`). A tool call whose `arguments` were absent OR were present and unparseable as JSON decoded to `{}`; a tool call whose `id` was absent decoded to `\"\"`; a `usage` object that was absent, non-numeric or missing one of its two counts decoded to `0`. Each arm is a different consequence rather than three spellings of one. The `{}` reaches `gunbc.harness.harness_tool`, which reads the tool's parameters off it and finds none. THE CONSEQUENCE THERE IS NARROWER THAN IT FIRST LOOKS AND THE CORRECTION IS WORTH CARRYING (side-chat review, 2026-09-11, against an earlier draft of this row that claimed an empty command executes): `harness_execute_tool_use` declares `command` required and refuses a call without it as `ToolInputMemberMissing`, so on today's one implemented tool nothing runs. What the fabrication actually produces is a MISATTRIBUTION -- the model's real arguments are discarded and the model is told back that it sent a call with no command, which is a fact about the codec reported as a fact about the model -- plus a spent round. The refusal is a property of run_command's single required member, not of the decoder: a tool with an optional or defaulted parameter would dispatch on the empty object, which is why the repair belongs in the decoder and not in the dispatcher. The `\"\"` is written back as the `tool_use_id` of the tool result, so the model is handed output it cannot attribute, and two calls in one round become indistinguishable. The `0` is compared by `harness_context_exhausted` and `harness_compaction_due` against the declared budget, so the two mechanisms that exist to stop a turn before it overruns its window are disarmed precisely when the usage object cannot be read.",

    "THE REPAIR'S OWN FAILURE MODE IS THE MIRROR OF THE CLASS, AND IT WAS WRITTEN BEFORE IT WAS CAUGHT (side-chat review, 2026-09-11). Making the string reader distinguish read / absent / duplicated left `null` in the malformed arm -- and the chat completion schema this decoder serves types the assistant message's `content` and its reasoning field as NULLABLE strings, so a TOOL-ONLY round, which is the round that matters, arrives as `\"content\": null` and was refused before its tool calls were decoded. The model's commands were then lost to a decoder defect rather than to a wire fault, which is this class's harm with the sign reversed: not a gap wearing the costume of data, but valid data refused as a gap. The repair is not leniency -- `null` is its own outcome, `StringNull`, distinct from absent, duplicated and wrong-typed, and each consumer decides what present-null means for ITS member, so the nullable two take a no-text arm and every required member still refuses. THE EVIDENCE HAS TO BE A PAIR: positive controls at `test.claim.harness_chat_shape` (null content beside tool_calls decodes the calls; null reasoning decodes) proving the over-refusal is gone, beside reds (a null tool_call id still refuses; a duplicated content member one of whose copies is null still refuses) proving the refusals were not widened into leniency to satisfy them. Either half alone is satisfiable by the wrong decoder.",

    "THE USAGE ARM SHOWS THE SECOND REPAIR SHAPE, AND WHY REFUSAL IS NOT ALWAYS THE ANSWER. A response whose content decoded perfectly but whose counts did not is TWO observations, one good and one missing; refusing the whole turn would throw away work the model did, and defaulting would fabricate a measurement. The repair is a typed unavailability carried to the consumer that must decide -- `HarnessUsageRead`, following the same shape the same module already used for the clock, whose `ClockUnixMillisRefused` rides into the event stream instead of a fabricated epoch. The line then stops at the budget check, which is the one consumer that cannot proceed, and the event stream records `round.usage_unavailable` rather than a `round.usage` of zeros that a throughput reader would difference into a plausible rate.",

    "RUNG. Found at mitigatable-and-not-even-that (no diagnostic existed; the arms were green by construction). Repaired to mechanically preventable: the decode arms refuse or return unavailability, and discriminating reds -- one per fabricated arm, each of which was a GREEN PARSE before the repair -- are enrolled at `test.claim.harness_chat_shape` beside positive controls proving well-formed bodies still decode and that an unmodelled block kind is still skipped rather than refused. **ENROLLMENT IS THE LOAD-BEARING HALF OF THAT SENTENCE AND WAS NEARLY WRITTEN WITHOUT IT** (review 63385, 2026-09-11). That module carries no prefix in `v2.workflow.required_floor` `required_gate_prefixes` and must not: the roster is the operator ruling that the required gate is the compiler floor and nothing else, and a harness wire codec is precisely what that ruling moved off the gate. So the module dispositioned `DeclinedOutsideRequiredGate` on every ordinary floor and ran only on pull requests that touched it (`PlannedAsChangedWitness`) -- which is not enrollment, and the dated proof is that the `unit:` parameter landed on `harness_decode_chat_completion` in #10815 while this module went on calling it with one argument, an arity error the floor has a blocking wall for, green for months. NO ENROLLMENT ROW WAS AUTHORED FOR IT EITHER, AND THAT IS A DECISION RATHER THAN AN OMISSION (manager ruling, 2026-09-11, after one was written and removed). The roster that decides the required floor is `required_gate_prefixes`, whose own header states that nothing on it is a product, fleet, deploy, secret, dashboard or roadmap witness because those are exactly what the operator's ruling moved off the gate; a harness wire codec is product, so the prefix does not belong there and the roster is left alone. The alternative tried first was a `CommitWitnessClaim` row on `gunbc.commit_workflow` `commit_gate_roster`, and it was deleted once measured: `v2.workflow.required_floor` `required_floor_site_disposition` decides membership from module-path prefixes alone and consults no roster, and `ci_floor_commit_witness_claim_schedule` with its `gunbc.ci_spec` projection `gunbc_ci_floor_witness_entries` has no consumer on the required-CI path. The discriminating artifact is the `required-floor-disposition` TSV of run 34564416008, where every `test.claim.harness_chat_shape` identity reads `planned_as_changed_witness` -- selected because the diff touched the file, not by enrollment. A roster row with no executing consumer is a DESIGN section 3c dangling declaration that READS AS COVERAGE, which is worse than no row at all, so it went. THE STANDING RUNG IS THEREFORE MITIGATABLE and the loss is not a gap of this class's own making: it is the declared drop `gunbc.rung_drop` `required_gate_bankruptcy`, whose population is named as every witness outside the roster, reported per run as `declined_outside_required_gate`, and whose restoration trigger is the capability of a required run whose population is DERIVED from the change with the whole corpus as its universe. This class's reds are in that population and are retired by that trigger, not by a row anyone here could write. CEILING: structural impossibility is attainable and not reached. The state is still writable because the decoder returns a domain value by hand; a codec DERIVED from the declared wire shape, where a required member has no constructor for 'not read', has no arm in which to write a default. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: a generated codec over `extdeps.llm.anthropic_messages_api` and the OpenAI chat shape -- emission and ingestion as one decision procedure read in both directions (DESIGN section 4) -- sufficient to replace every hand-authored decode arm in `gunbc.harness.harness_wire`, not merely to cover the response envelope.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
